{"duration_api_ms":252503,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"301a3ab4-c7cf-4d8f-a84c-20c7a89839ac","total_cost_usd":0.29992599999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15428,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":23821,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17474},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15428,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":23821,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15428,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15428},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":23821,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15428,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.29992599999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":17474,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is one line: D=3.38, bluntness 1.25, cone 70 (its upper bound), with only gamma varied from -1.55 to -3.58. Its ends are (241.5 kW/m2, 419.9 K) and (290.5 kW/m2, 393.3 K). Peak g depends almost only on gamma, roughly 1.67 g per degree, and hits the 12 g limit near gamma of -3.60. The mass-fraction margin is near zero (0.0046) at D=3.38, b=1.25. Bluntness is capped by geometry at cone 70. Fitting the failed-geometry message (C-15633e2cd134) gives an exact feasibility rule: nose radius = b*D, shoulder radius = 0.1*D, and cos(cone) <= 0.8/(2b-0.2). At cone 70 this caps b at about 1.2695. Hypervolume is dominated by bondline temperature, since heat flux is small against its 2.5 MW/m2 reference. The remaining gains are small: shift the whole line slightly toward larger D, larger b and the g-limited gamma.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-a7c35d14bbab, C-e8cf251744f0, C-cb4f7a3f0bb6, C-169e7d6af794: g runs 11.435, 11.837, 11.919, 11.969 at gamma -3.25, -3.5, -3.55, -3.58. C-57441bbcc2d0 (D=3.34, gamma -3.6) has g=11.986, so D=3.38 at -3.6 would be about 12.00 and infeasible.\",\"C-2081e8b0eca2, C-98a7507c3b9c, C-57441bbcc2d0, C-e8cf251744f0: mass margin is 0.0105, 0.0164, 0.0280 and 0.0046 at D=3.37, 3.36, 3.34, 3.38. That is about 0.59 per metre of D. It does not depend on gamma.\",\"C-1b3ade12fa06 vs C-6f66fc14536a: b 1.25 to 1.26 lowers q by about 420 W/m2 and T by 0.06 K, and raises mass margin from 0.004613 to 0.004924, about 0.031 per unit b.\",\"C-a903a9aa40d3 (b=1.0, D=3.38) has mass margin -0.0024, and C-224b7254a7ae (D=3.4, b=1.22) has -0.0081. Both fit the linear D and b sensitivities.\",\"C-15633e2cd134 (D=3.15, b=1.25, cone 69) fails with a fore-cone length of -14.659 mm. The formula R*(0.8+0.2cos(theta)-2b*cos(theta))/tan(theta) reproduces this to 0.01 mm. It predicts b=1.25 is fine at cone 70 and b up to about 1.2695 is still valid.\",\"C-f9dcc6deb7b1 (D=3.74, gamma -5.44, T=377.8 K) violates both g (15.5) and mass fraction (-0.31). Lower T therefore needs a larger D or steeper gamma, and the g and mass limits block both.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak g is set by entry velocity and gamma. The g limit therefore fixes the steepest usable gamma at about -3.59, and this is the lowest-T end of the front. At fixed gamma, T and q fall with a larger nose radius (b*D) and a lower ballistic coefficient (larger D). Mass fraction grows roughly with D^2 and falls slightly with b. Cone 70 gives the best Cd and the smallest shield, so the optimum sits at the joint corner: cone 70, b near 1.265 (geometry limit), D just under the mass limit (about 3.386-3.388), gamma near -3.59. I estimate the shifts from finite differences in the data: about -42 kW/m2 per unit b, -125 kW/m2 per metre of D, and -17 K per metre of D on T. This relies on local linearity plus prior ballistic-entry knowledge that g is independent of ballistic coefficient. The same shifted geometry with gamma swept from -1.5 to -3.55 should give a front that dominates the current one. I add a few low-cost probes of cone angle at lower b, where the geometry stays valid, to check that the cone effect is small.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The mass margin at D=3.385-3.388 is only 0.0005-0.002, and the g margin at gamma -3.59 to -3.595 is 0.0003-0.001, so some corner points may fall infeasible. The linear extrapolations of the b and D sensitivities could be slightly off. I have no direct data on the cone-angle effect on q and T away from cone 70, so the exploration probes carry high uncertainty. The geometry rule was fitted from a single failure message, so points with b near 1.268 carry some risk of a geometry failure.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-169e7d6af794\",\"rationale\":\"Move the current best corner to a slightly larger D and b, keeping gamma at the g limit (about 11.99 g).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.386,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.265,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.59},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":289400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.95,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the larger D and b lower T at the g-limited corner, which drives most of the hypervolume. Margins are thin: mass about 0.001, g about 0.001.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-169e7d6af794\",\"rationale\":\"Push gamma to the g limit with a slightly smaller D for extra mass margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.265,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.595},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":289500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g boundary precisely. Predicted g is about 11.996, with a margin near 0.0003.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-169e7d6af794\",\"rationale\":\"Use the maximum D and b that the mass and geometry estimates allow.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.388,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.268,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.585},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":289100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the joint mass and geometry boundary. The predicted fore-cone length is about 0.2 mm and the mass margin about 0.0005.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-169e7d6af794\",\"rationale\":\"Safe fallback at the corner with D reduced for extra mass margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.265,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.59},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":291400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.25,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Guarantees a feasible point near the corner and calibrates the D sensitivity.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb4f7a3f0bb6\",\"rationale\":\"Shifted-front point at gamma -3.55.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.265,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":288400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.36,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A robust front point that dominates the old front point at -3.55.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e8cf251744f0\",\"rationale\":\"Shifted-front point at gamma -3.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.265,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":287130,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.86,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves on C-e8cf251744f0 in both objectives.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e8cf251744f0\",\"rationale\":\"Fills the gap between -3.4 and -3.5 on the shifted front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.265,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285880,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.37,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front near the low-T end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-fe378e1d3bfd\",\"rationale\":\"Shifted-front point at gamma -3.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.265,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":282100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the improvement to mid-front points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a7c35d14bbab\",\"rationale\":\"Shifted-front point at gamma -3.15.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.265,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.15},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":278300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-71dbb7df9fb4\",\"rationale\":\"Shifted-front point at gamma -3.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.265,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274570,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Mid-front point that dominates C-71dbb7df9fb4.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d6f59a05633b\",\"rationale\":\"Shifted-front point at gamma -2.75.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.265,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":268320,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves the mid-front and reduces staircase loss.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-c601b2439f28\",\"rationale\":\"Shifted-front point at gamma -2.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.265,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":262150,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves the mid-front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-150ba7f34298\",\"rationale\":\"Shifted-front point at gamma -2.25.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.265,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":256100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves the shallow-mid front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6d99358fc11d\",\"rationale\":\"Shifted-front point at gamma -2.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.265,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":250240,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":412.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves the shallow end of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3e63825a6a3b\",\"rationale\":\"Shifted-front point at gamma -1.75.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.265,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":244650,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves the shallow end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-034277f4c3be\",\"rationale\":\"Extends the front to the minimum gamma of -1.5, which gives the lowest q.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.265,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":239400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":420.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the low-q end of the front beyond the current best q of 241.5 kW/m2.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b460a0993d3f\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the cone effect at 69 deg with b=1.2, close to the corner.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":293000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether a slightly smaller cone changes q, T or mass margin. Geometry margin is fine (b limit at 69 deg is 1.216).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-006844c44839\",\"rationale\":\"Probe a cone of 66 deg with b=1.05, which is within the geometry limit of 1.083.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.05,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":301500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Measures the cone-angle effect on q, T and mass margin, and whether lower cones offer any advantage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-006844c44839\",\"rationale\":\"Probe a cone of 60 deg with b=0.85 (geometry limit 0.9).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.85,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":60.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":322000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the trend for smaller cone angle and bluntness, and whether mass margin behaves differently than the linear model predicts.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-006844c44839\",\"rationale\":\"Probe a moderate cone of 45 deg with b=0.6 (geometry limit 0.666).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.6,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":45.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":345000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Broad exploration of a different geometry family to confirm that it is dominated, or to find an unexpected gain in Cd or mass.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-006844c44839\",\"rationale\":\"Probe a cone of 55 deg with b=0.75 (geometry limit 0.797) and gamma -3.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.75,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":55.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":323000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a second data point for the cone and bluntness trend to check the linear sensitivity model away from the corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":203408,"type":"result","duration_ms":252548,"uuid":"019ae73f-3fbf-44cc-985e-f000ecc31a69","ttft_stream_ms":1194,"time_to_request_ms":32,"first_content_frame_ms":1194,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
